---
source: crates/instrukt-cli/tests/layered-configuration.rs
expression: "read(&[\"config\", \"get\"])"
---
modules:
  blueprint: false
  todos: false
  events: false
  history: true
ticks: 'on'
github:
  api_url: https://api.github.com
runner:
  autostart: false
  runtime: t3
runtimes:
  t3:
    dispatch: 'Use native delegated-task dispatch with shared isolation from this conversation, preserving its recorded workspace. Each phase has its own recorded worktree: preparation shares <slug>/prepare, while the later work phase shares <slug>/work. All children inherit their orchestrator''s phase workspace. Use the supplied brief, semantic key, title, role-attempt facts and resolved selection.profile, selection.kind, selection.instance, selection.model, selection.effort and selection.options. Pass the resolved provider/model and provider-native effort/options to native delegation; do not substitute project defaults. Include the role/attempt identity in the child brief and require it to await confirmed instrukt binding before workspace changes, record writes or stamps. Retain the native child/task id and matching workspace/branch/head evidence for instrukt binding. Follow native completion delivery.'
    message_child: Use native child/task messaging or continuation for the supplied child id. Relay the bounded follow-up and retain the same role/attempt. Continue an idle child through the native continuation operation.
    message_peer: Use native thread messaging for the supplied peer/coordinator thread id and text. Preserve its identity and the message's attribution.
    read_thread: Read the identified thread with native thread-read operations, including the relevant message range and attribution. Report pagination or unavailable evidence; read no archive/history service.
    inspect_thread: Read the identified native thread or own delegated task through its native status/result operation. Follow native completion/wake instructions; inspect a running task only when those instructions permit it.
    look_around: Use native project thread listing and available current-thread metadata filters. Select the requested project and include settled threads when needed. Retain the runtime's visibility limits for children; listing absence proves no missing child.
    steer: Use native thread/child input with its supported steering mode. Preserve the running turn and children. For a target that queues rather than interjects, hand over now for its next supported turn.
    discuss: When asked to open a discussion, use instrukt discuss open <thread> with optional --message <text>. The native caller is your thread. Use instrukt discuss close with optional --message <text> to send a final contribution before closing for both members. These commands manage the conversation link; the long-lived instrukt runner automatically relays finished human and agent turns. Focused roles report through their own output/artifacts; workers report upward through native child-result delivery.
    start_thread: Use the supplied placement.title verbatim as the thread title. Use the supplied placement.selection profile, kind, instance, model, effort and options for native startup. A host CLI start passes --provider <provider> --model <model>; effort/options have no CLI flags and remain explicit start evidence. Fetch origin before each new phase branch, then for a preparation orchestrator start t3 thread start <project> - --worktree origin/main --branch <slug>/prepare --title <display-title>. After reviewed docs integrate to main, the integrator removes that worktree and deletes the prepare branch locally and on origin. Fetch origin again and start work later from origin/main with --worktree origin/main --branch <slug>/work; on another computer use --worktree origin/<slug>/work --branch <slug>/work. instrukt derives these names; creation refuses an existing local branch. Native shared children inherit the phase worktree. After deliberate native startup, enter todo prepare/work with --placement-evidence containing native session, key, title, recorded worktree, branch, head and source; shell cwd alone is not placement evidence. Wake a settled retained orchestrator in place. The CLI cannot attach an existing worktree to a replacement thread; resolve that placement or use native MCP existing-worktree start. Ad hoc work uses its own one-off worktree; only the integrator writes main.
    cancel_child: Use native delegated-task cancellation for the supplied own-child task id, preserving its branch, workspace and unfinished evidence. Read the returned cancellation state before deciding its remaining work.
    finish_thread: Use native settling for the addressed thread; settling this conversation applies when its current turn ends. Preserve unfinished human and worker obligations before settling.
    discover_environments: Use the connection's native linked-environment discovery. Match participating computers to observed environment ids and registered project paths, keeping instrukt machine IDs distinct. Report missing mappings and access.
    connect_environment: Use native environment linking with the named computer as its hint and follow the connection's authentication flow. Report any unresolved operator prerequisite.
    dispatch_remote: Use the connection's native task operation explicitly targeting the identified linked environment and registered project. Supply the local configuration brief, skill package location/text and report destination; preserve local permission limits. Follow its completion instructions and compare returned verification across computers, retaining partial success.
schema_version: 5
agents: {}
board: false
approvals:
  prd: human
  task: human
workflow:
  domain: sdlc
ci:
  dependency_branch_prefixes:
  - renovate/
project: hostile
